// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- row 11
// Starting a match from the lobby (PS3 1.19 t008): the leader presses Start, the lobby checks the party against the
// net game's player limits and teams, prepares the match and shows the 5-second "starting" countdown.
//
// Counters: ext+0x2238 cd[0] presses, [1] / [2] the countdown's start time and text, [3] the party told, [4] / [5]
// countdown shown / not shown (then the match starts at once), [6] why the checks refused (2 party too big, 3 too few
// players, 4 teams; with the counted players and the per-team counts above), [7] party size, type and limits.
//
//  * u3x_popup_timed(base, s, text, seconds, ok, cancel): shows the menu's timed popup (0x453470dd) with `text`,
//    ending after `seconds` (300 engine ticks each), its buttons set to ok / cancel (the menu's own buttons kept once,
//    for the C side to put back); 1 when shown.
//  * u3x_start_checks(base, s): the party fits: no more players than the net game allows; at least its minimum (unless
//    a lone player may start alone - flag 0x80, for type 18 only with 0x20000 - or the minimum is off, 0x80000, which
//    is counted in sc[1]); for team games (type 10), not everybody on one team. A refusal shows its dialog.
//  * u3x_start_game(base, s): Start pressed: party guests can't start; the online lobby or the m03 flow can take it;
//    the selection is committed; flag 0x40 starts at once; otherwise (with the game's start native, net mode 2, LAN
//    or online) not while a start of the last 30 s is still under way or the countdown is up, then the checks, the
//    preparation, the party told, and the countdown (or the start).
//  * u3x_start_prepare(base, s): the match's preparation: our net commands reset when the game's command list is
//    ours, the match state reset (unless flag 0x20000000), the playlist "san-upper-multi-killvis" without its
//    kill-visibility value unless flag 8, and the LAN session re-attached.
//  * u3x_start_game_now(base, s): prepares and starts at once (not while the network is already starting, state 3
//    or 0xb).
