// Pieces of the animation-state message (PS3 1.19 anim pack, b119): the bit stream writer, locators (position +
// rotation quaternion, 8 floats) and their maths in the game's float steps, bound frames, and the lookups of
// animations in the actor's art groups and in the streaming animation roots.
//
//  * u3x_bsw(bs, val, n): appends the low n bits of val (highest first) to the bit stream {u32 words *, bit position,
//    bit capacity}; past the capacity it sets the replication error instead.
//  * u3x_fabs(f): |f| of a float's bits.
//  * u3x_bsw_vec(bs, v): a vector: flag 0 and 18 / 17 / 18-bit fixed point (x and z * 512, y * 256) when it is
//    within +-255 / +-127 / +-255, else flag 1 and the three floats.
//  * u3x_bsw_frame(base, bs, f): a frame through the game's writer, when 512 bits are left (else the error).
//  * u3x_q_mul / u3x_q_rot: quaternion product a*b (x, y, z, w) and the rotation of v by q (q * v * q').
//  * u3x_loc_mul(o, a, b): b in a's space put into the world (a after b); u3x_loc_rel(o, a, b): b seen from a.
//  * u3x_bf_world(base, f, o): a bound frame's world locator: its parent's (the bound object's, while the handle is
//    valid, else the frame's own copy at +0x20) after its local one (+0x40).
//  * u3x_bind_root(base, obj): the object the actor's binding hangs on: from the object's own binding upwards (at most
//    64 parents) until an object with flag 0x800.
//  * u3x_ev_query(base, sid, obj): the game's event query `sid` on obj (first result word).
//  * u3x_np_by_id(base, id): the network player (of 10) with code id.
//  * u3x_tab_find(t, key): binary search of a table of 16-byte entries sorted by their first word (-1 = none).
//  * u3x_art_tab(g): an art group's animation table.
//  * u3x_sid(base, s): the game's string id of a name (0 for none).
//  * u3x_anim_lookup(base, tab, idx, id, anim, tabs): finds animation id: in the actor's 8 art groups (only the group
//    named like the animation's art group, when given), else in the art group of that name (then *tab is its id).
//  * u3x_stream_root(base, x, phase): the streaming animation (of up to 50 roots) that plays x, and its phase.
