// Respawning in multiplayer (PS3 1.19 respawn path, b020/b021): object handles, clocks, the current net game, co-op and
// late-join tests, whether a player is alive, the respawn delay in ticks, the game's type objects, and choosing a
// spawner: its locator, the fade, the streaming request for its region and whether its levels are loaded.
//
// Counters: s+0x3d40 rs[7] region requests, rs[8] levels asked; s+0x3d78 rs2[0] switches (bit 2: no fade), rs2[3] /
// rs2[4] fades and the last one, rs2[5] / rs2[6] levels and dropped ones, rs2[7] spawns refused (no spawner).
//
//  * u3x_handle_obj_valid(h) / u3x_handle_obj(h): a game handle {object **, id} still names its object (+0x7c).
//  * u3x_net_now / u3x_loc_now(base): the network and local clocks.
//  * u3x_netgame_cur(base, s) / u3x_netgame_type(base, s): the current net game entry (0xd0 bytes) of the menu's net-game
//    table, and its type.
//  * u3x_net_coop_mode(base, s): multiplayer runs a co-op type: the match manager's current net game (+0x661c) tested
//    with the game's own type mask (u3x_type_is_coop) = types 4, 8, 9, 11, 13, 16, 17, 18 (mask 0x72b1 from type 4).
//  * u3x_net_late_joining(base): this PC joins a running match (match room, not its host, net phase past 3).
//  * u3x_np_has_effect(s, p, h) / u3x_np_alive(s, p): a net player's effect; alive: the "alive" effect, its character
//    still there with health within its maximum, or its "alive" byte.
