// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- row 25
// The Cinema HUD's draw half (PS3 1.19 f_667f0c, b024/b026): the tab bar of row 13 on its dark panel, the pulsing
// cursor, the tab icons with their labels (measured, then centred under the icon and kept inside the panel), and the
// film's progress bar with its head, the clip markers (cuts red, other kinds grey), the current / total time, the film
// name and, while the film doesn't run at normal speed, the speed ("x%2.1f").
//
// Drawing goes through the game's own functions with the PS4 calling convention (u3x_k26_call): the panel (0x640ac0 /
// 0x63d6f0), sprites (0x11b8dd0), textured or plain quads (0xe42310), texts (0xf1d9f0), localized texts (0xf32ae0),
// textures (0x11b89b0), snprintf (0x139cab0) and the film's current second (0x6a2700). All values are float bits, and
// every step is the game's own float operation in the game's order.
// Counters eb[220] draws, [221] refused / bad entries, [222] visible tabs, [223] / [224] current second / film length,
// [225] labels, [226] markers, [227] marker guard, [228] speed texts, [229] screenshot skips; eb[243..246] the panel,
// eb[46] plain panels, eb[47] / eb[63] its corner.
//
//  * u3x_k26_call(c): calls c->fn with 6 integer, 5 float (xmm0..4) and 2 stack arguments and the vector count (al).
//  * u3x_k26_f2d / fsel / rd / c4 / col: float to double bits, PPC fsel (a >= 0 ? b : c, NaN -> c), a float load,
//    a colour, and a colour packed as a<<24 | b<<16 | g<<8 | r (each clamped to 0..1, times 255).
//  * u3x_k26_tp(P): default text parameters. u3x_k26_text / str / sprite / tex / quad / time: the drawing calls; time
//    formats seconds as "h:mm:ss" or "m:ss" with the game's format strings.
//  * u3x_k26_callees(b): the game functions used are the expected ones (checked once).
//  * u3x_k26_draw(b, el, rbp): draws the bar of element el (row 13 layout); rbp is the HUD draw's frame (its draw
//    context at rbp-0x11f8; context 0 unless eb[1] bit 0x40000).
